From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:14:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini-station: let the CCI follow
 without required-opps

The first station-dvfs run stopped when cpufreq-dt loaded. CPU4-7 boot
at 1274 MHz, which the L table does not list, so cpufreq moves them to
1352 MHz at once. That change failed with -EBUSY: the CPU points required
CCI points, and the OPP core refuses to set a table whose required
tables are not yet linked, before mtk-cci-devfreq has loaded. The core
then hit its BUG for an unlisted frequency it could not leave. Loading
mtk-cci-devfreq first is not possible, because its passive governor
needs the cpufreq policies.

Drop the required-opps. The passive governor then maps each cluster's
place in its range onto the CCI's range, and the faster cluster wins.
The CCI still sets the voltage of its own point, so VPROC1 stays high
enough for it.

Keep VSRAM_L at 1.10 V or above. That is where the firmware leaves it
with VPROC1 at 1.00 V, 90 mV above the vendor kernel's VPROC1 + 10 mV
rule.
